                },
                "category": "offensive",
                "description": {
                    "value": "<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The bogeyman has killed a creature within the last round and is adjacent to its corpse</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> The bogeyman consumes the creature's soul. The soul is utterly destroyed—nothing short of a @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Wish] ritual or similar magic can restore it to life, and only after the bogeyman has been slain. The bogey regains Hit Points equal to double the level of the consumed creature. After devouring 10 souls within a year, it increases its level by 1, and its statistics improve accordingly.</p>"
                },
